<td><a href="/wiki/Heal_Ball" title="Heal Ball">Heal Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #B7A3C3; border: 1px solid #5E4A6A; text-align: center" data-sort-value="4"><b>IV</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="14">14
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x0E
</td>
<td>1×
</td>
<td>Fully restores a caught Pokémon's <a href="/wiki/Stat#HP" title="Stat">HP</a> and <a href="/wiki/PP" title="PP">PP</a> and removes their <a href="/wiki/Status_condition" title="Status condition">status conditions</a>.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Quick_Ball" title="Quick Ball"><img alt="Quick Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/7/72/Bag_Quick_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Quick_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/7/72/Bag_Quick_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Quick_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/7/72/Bag_Quick_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Quick_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Quick_Ball" title="Quick Ball">Quick Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #B7A3C3; border: 1px solid #5E4A6A; text-align: center" data-sort-value="4"><b>IV</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="15">15
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x0F
</td>
<td>5× if used on the first turn of a battle<br />1× otherwise
</td>
<td>In <a href="/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Legends:_Z-A" title="Pokémon Legends: Z-A">Pokémon Legends: Z-A</a>, the increased catch rate is instead applied if neither the wild Pokémon nor the player's active Pokémon have used any moves since the beginning of the battle.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Cherish_Ball" title="Cherish Ball"><img alt="Cherish Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/8/8f/Bag_Cherish_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Cherish_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/8/8f/Bag_Cherish_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Cherish_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/8/8f/Bag_Cherish_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Cherish_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Cherish_Ball" title="Cherish Ball">Cherish Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #B7A3C3; border: 1px solid #5E4A6A; text-align: center" data-sort-value="4"><b>IV</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="16">16
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x10
</td>
<td>1×
</td>
<td>Unobtainable by the player, but used for various <a href="/wiki/Event_Pok%C3%A9mon" title="Event Pokémon">event Pokémon</a>.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Fast_Ball" title="Fast Ball"><img alt="Fast Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/3/3c/Bag_Fast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Fast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/3/3c/Bag_Fast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Fast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/3/3c/Bag_Fast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Fast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Fast_Ball" title="Fast Ball">Fast Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #DCD677; border: 1px solid #837D1E; text-align: center" data-sort-value="2"><b>II</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="17">17
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x11
</td>
<td>4× if used on a Pokémon with a base <a href="/wiki/Stat#Speed" title="Stat">Speed</a> <a href="/wiki/Category:Pok%C3%A9mon_whose_base_Speed_stat_is_greater_than_100" title="Category:Pokémon whose base Speed stat is greater than 100">of at least 100</a><br />1× otherwise
</td>
<td>In <a href="/wiki/Generation_II" title="Generation II">Generation II</a>, it was intended to have a 4× catch modifier for Pokémon that can <a href="/wiki/Escape#Wild_Pokémon" title="Escape">flee</a>, but it only does for three of them: <a href="/wiki/Magnemite_(Pok%C3%A9mon)" title="Magnemite (Pokémon)">Magnemite</a>, <a href="/wiki/Grimer_(Pok%C3%A9mon)" title="Grimer (Pokémon)">Grimer</a> and <a href="/wiki/Tangela_(Pok%C3%A9mon)" title="Tangela (Pokémon)">Tangela</a>.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Level_Ball" title="Level Ball"><img alt="Level Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/f/f1/Bag_Level_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Level_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/f/f1/Bag_Level_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Level_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/f/f1/Bag_Level_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Level_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Level_Ball" title="Level Ball">Level Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #DCD677; border: 1px solid #837D1E; text-align: center" data-sort-value="2"><b>II</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="18">18
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x12
</td>
<td>1× if the player's Pokémon is the same level as or a lower level than the wild Pokémon<br />2× if the player's Pokémon is at a higher level than the wild Pokémon but less than double it<br />4× if the player's Pokémon is more than double but less than four times the level of the wild Pokémon<br />8× if the player's Pokémon is of a level four times or more than that of the wild Pokémon
</td>
<td>In <a href="/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Legends:_Z-A" title="Pokémon Legends: Z-A">Pokémon Legends: Z-A</a>, if the player does not have a Pokémon out, the Level Ball will always have a catch rate modifier of 1×.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Lure_Ball" title="Lure Ball"><img alt="Lure Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/f/f4/Bag_Lure_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Lure_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/f/f4/Bag_Lure_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Lure_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/f/f4/Bag_Lure_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Lure_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Lure_Ball" title="Lure Ball">Lure Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #DCD677; border: 1px solid #837D1E; text-align: center" data-sort-value="2"><b>II</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="19">19
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x13
</td>
<td>4× if used on a Pokémon encountered while <a href="/wiki/Fishing" title="Fishing">fishing</a><br />1× otherwise
</td>
<td>In <a href="/wiki/Johto" title="Johto">Johto</a>, the bonus was 3x while in <a href="/wiki/Alola" title="Alola">Alola</a>, the bonus was 5x<br />In <a href="/wiki/Generation_IX" title="Generation IX">Generation IX</a>, it instead had an increased catch rate if used on Pokémon that are currently on or in water.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Heavy_Ball" title="Heavy Ball"><img alt="Heavy Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/46/Bag_Heavy_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Heavy_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/46/Bag_Heavy_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Heavy_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/46/Bag_Heavy_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Heavy_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Heavy_Ball" title="Heavy Ball">Heavy Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #DCD677; border: 1px solid #837D1E; text-align: center" data-sort-value="2"><b>II</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="20">20
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x14
</td>
<td>-20 if used on a Pokémon weighing <a href="/wiki/List_of_Pok%C3%A9mon_by_weight#218.3_lbs._to_220.2_lbs._(99.0_kg_to_99.9_kg)" title="List of Pokémon by weight">220.2&#160;lbs. (99.9&#160;kg)</a> or less<br />±0 if used on a Pokémon weighing <a href="/wiki/List_of_Pok%C3%A9mon_by_weight#220.5_lbs._to_225.5_lbs._(100.0_kg_to_102.3_kg)" title="List of Pokémon by weight">220.5&#160;lbs. (100.0&#160;kg)</a> – <a href="/wiki/List_of_Pok%C3%A9mon_by_weight#330.7_lbs._to_440.7_lbs._(150.0_kg_to_199.9_kg)" title="List of Pokémon by weight">440.7&#160;lbs. (199.9&#160;kg)</a><br />+20 if used on a Pokémon weighing <a href="/wiki/List_of_Pok%C3%A9mon_by_weight#440.9_lbs._to_451.3_lbs._(200.0_kg_to_204.7_kg)" title="List of Pokémon by weight">440.9&#160;lbs. (200.0&#160;kg)</a> – <a href="/wiki/List_of_Pok%C3%A9mon_by_weight#617.3_lbs._to_661.2_lbs._(280.0_kg_to_299.9_kg)" title="List of Pokémon by weight">661.2&#160;lbs. (299.9&#160;kg)</a><br />+30 if used on a Pokémon weighing <a href="/wiki/List_of_Pok%C3%A9mon_by_weight#661.4_lbs._to_677.0_lbs._(300.0_kg_to_307.1_kg)" title="List of Pokémon by weight">661.4&#160;lbs. (300.0&#160;kg)</a> or more
</td>
<td>In <a href="/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Crystal_Version" title="Pokémon Crystal Version">Pokémon Crystal</a> only, there is a glitch that causes the retrieved weights of Pokémon whose index numbers are divisible by 64 (<a href="/wiki/Kadabra_(Pok%C3%A9mon)" title="Kadabra (Pokémon)">Kadabra</a>, <a href="/wiki/Tauros_(Pok%C3%A9mon)" title="Tauros (Pokémon)">Tauros</a>, and <a href="/wiki/Sunflora_(Pok%C3%A9mon)" title="Sunflora (Pokémon)">Sunflora</a>) to become junk data that are, in turn, interpreted as massive weights, causing these particular Pokémon to receive the +40 capture modifier.<br />In <a href="/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Sun_and_Moon" title="Pokémon Sun and Moon">Pokémon Sun and Moon</a> only, a Heavy Ball will always fail to catch a Pokémon whose weight is less than 220.46&#160;lbs (100.0&#160;kg) and whose catch rate is less than or equal to 20. This is because the game will set the catch rate to 0 when the catch rate becomes negative due to the -20 modifier that is applied.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Love_Ball" title="Love Ball"><img alt="Love Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/40/Bag_Love_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Love_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/40/Bag_Love_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Love_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/40/Bag_Love_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Love_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Love_Ball" title="Love Ball">Love Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #DCD677; border: 1px solid #837D1E; text-align: center" data-sort-value="2"><b>II</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="21">21
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x15
</td>
<td>8× if used on a Pokémon of the same species but opposite gender of the player's Pokémon<br />1× otherwise
</td>
<td>In <a href="/wiki/Generation_II" title="Generation II">Generation II</a>, it has an 8× catch modifier if both Pokémon are the same species <i>and</i> gender.<br />In <a href="/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Legends:_Z-A" title="Pokémon Legends: Z-A">Pokémon Legends: Z-A</a>, if the player does not have a Pokémon out, the Love Ball will always have a catch rate modifier of 1×.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Friend_Ball" title="Friend Ball"><img alt="Friend Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/4c/Bag_Friend_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Friend_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/4c/Bag_Friend_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Friend_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/4c/Bag_Friend_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Friend_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Friend_Ball" title="Friend Ball">Friend Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #DCD677; border: 1px solid #837D1E; text-align: center" data-sort-value="2"><b>II</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="22">22
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x16
</td>
<td>1×
</td>
<td>Sets caught Pokémon's <a href="/wiki/Friendship" title="Friendship">friendship</a> to 200<sup><a href="/wiki/Generation_II" title="Generation II">Gen II</a>-<a href="/wiki/Generation_VII" title="Generation VII">VII</a></sup>, or 150<sup><a href="/wiki/Generation_VIII" title="Generation VIII">Gen VIII</a>+</sup>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Moon_Ball" title="Moon Ball"><img alt="Moon Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/2/26/Bag_Moon_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Moon_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/2/26/Bag_Moon_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Moon_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/2/26/Bag_Moon_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Moon_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Moon_Ball" title="Moon Ball">Moon Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #DCD677; border: 1px solid #837D1E; text-align: center" data-sort-value="2"><b>II</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="23">23
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x17
</td>
<td>4× if used on a Pokémon that evolves by using a <a href="/wiki/Moon_Stone" title="Moon Stone">Moon Stone</a><br />1× otherwise
</td>
<td>In <a href="/wiki/Generation_II" title="Generation II">Generation II</a>, it always has a 1× catch modifier due to a <a href="/wiki/List_of_glitches_in_Generation_II#Catch_rate" title="List of glitches in Generation II">programming error</a>.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Sport_Ball" title="Sport Ball"><img alt="Sport Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/6/68/Bag_Sport_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Sport_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/6/68/Bag_Sport_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Sport_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/6/68/Bag_Sport_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Sport_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Sport_Ball" title="Sport Ball">Sport Ball</a><span class="explain" title="Park Ball in Generation II">*</span>
</td>
<td style="background: #DCD677; border: 1px solid #537A13; text-align: center" data-sort-value="2"><b>II</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="24">24
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x18
</td>
<td><span class="explain" title="1.5× prior to Generation VIII">1×</span>
</td>
<td>Prior to <a href="/wiki/Generation_VIII" title="Generation VIII">Generation VIII</a>, it was only usable during the <a href="/wiki/Bug-Catching_Contest" title="Bug-Catching Contest">Bug-Catching Contest</a>.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Dream_Ball" title="Dream Ball"><img alt="Dream Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/6/6a/Bag_Dream_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Dream_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/6/6a/Bag_Dream_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Dream_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/6/6a/Bag_Dream_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Dream_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Dream_Ball" title="Dream Ball">Dream Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #9FCADF; border: 1px solid #467186; text-align: center" data-sort-value="5"><b>V</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="25">25
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x19
</td>
<td>4× if used on a <a href="/wiki/Sleep_(status_condition)" title="Sleep (status condition)">sleeping</a> or <a href="/wiki/Status_condition#Drowsy" title="Status condition">drowsy</a> Pokémon<br />1× otherwise
</td>
<td>Used only in <a href="/wiki/Entralink" title="Entralink">Entree Forest</a> prior to <a href="/wiki/Generation_VIII" title="Generation VIII">Generation VIII</a>.<br />Guaranteed capture in <a href="/wiki/Generation_V" title="Generation V">Generation V</a>.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Beast_Ball" title="Beast Ball"><img alt="Beast Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/d/d1/Bag_Beast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Beast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/d/d1/Bag_Beast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Beast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/d/d1/Bag_Beast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Beast_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Beast_Ball" title="Beast Ball">Beast Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #E89483; border: 1px solid #8F3B2A; text-align: center" data-sort-value="6"><b>VII</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="26">26
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x1A
</td>
<td>5× if used on an <a href="/wiki/Ultra_Beast" title="Ultra Beast">Ultra Beast</a><br />0.1× otherwise
</td>
<td>If any other Poké Ball (except the Master Ball) is used on an Ultra Beast, it has a 0.1× catch modifier.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Park_Ball" title="Park Ball"><img alt="Park Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/6/63/Bag_Park_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Park_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/6/63/Bag_Park_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Park_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/6/63/Bag_Park_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Park_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Park_Ball" title="Park Ball">Park Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #B7A3C3; border: 1px solid #5E4A6A; text-align: center" data-sort-value="4"><b>IV</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="27"><span class="explain" title="Prior to Brilliant Diamond and Shining Pearl, the Park Ball occupied this index value. This index value was reallocated to the Strange Ball, games released from BDSP onwards have no programmed index number for the Park Ball.">27</span>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x1B
</td>
<td>N/A (guaranteed capture if used in <a href="/wiki/Pal_Park" title="Pal Park">Pal Park</a>)<br /><span class="explain" title="If used outside of Pal Park, the game will behave as if the player had thrown a standard Poké Ball instead.">1× otherwise</span>
</td>
<td>Unobtainable by the player, but used in <a href="/wiki/Pal_Park" title="Pal Park">Pal Park</a>.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/Strange_Ball" title="Strange Ball"><img alt="Strange Ball" src="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/48/Bag_Strange_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/40px-Bag_Strange_Ball_SV_Sprite.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="40" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/48/Bag_Strange_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/60px-Bag_Strange_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 1.5x, https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/thumb/4/48/Bag_Strange_Ball_SV_Sprite.png/80px-Bag_Strange_Ball_SV_Sprite.png 2x" data-file-width="160" data-file-height="160" /></a></span>
</td>
<td><a href="/wiki/Strange_Ball" title="Strange Ball">Strange Ball</a>
</td>
<td style="background: #C97DC0; border: 1px solid #702467; text-align: center" data-sort-value="7"><b>VIII</b>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center" data-sort-value="27"><span class="explain" title="Starting in Brilliant Diamond and Shining Pearl, the Strange Ball was assigned this index number, replacing the Park Ball. From BDSP onwards, the Park Ball has no programmed index number, with the Strange Ball occupying its previous value.">27</span>
</td>
<td style="text-align: center">0x1B
</td>
<td><span class="explain" title="Defaults to Poké Ball (Hisui) catchrate in Legends: Arceus if obtained via cheating; has no catchrate in BDSP due to a lack of item data.">0.75×</span>
</td>
<td>Unobtainable by the player. Pokémon in <a href="/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Legends:_Arceus" title="Pokémon Legends: Arceus">Pokémon Legends: Arceus</a> that were transferred from other games via <a href="/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_HOME" title="Pokémon HOME">Pokémon HOME</a>, as well as Pokémon from Legends: Arceus in <a href="/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Brilliant_Diamond_and_Shining_Pearl" title="Pokémon Brilliant Diamond and Shining Pearl">Pokémon Brilliant Diamond and Shining Pearl</a> or <a href="/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Scarlet_and_Violet" title="Pokémon Scarlet and Violet">Pokémon Scarlet and Violet</a> will be displayed in this ball.
</td></tr>
